# Per-entry overrides for recoll's system mimemap
# (/usr/share/recoll/examples/mimemap). Entries here replace the system value
# for the same extension; everything else is still inherited, so this file only
# needs the lines that are wrong.
#
# .ts ships as video/MP2T (MPEG-2 transport stream). That is defensible for a
# media indexer and completely wrong here: ~/Code has 10k+ TypeScript files and
# zero transport streams. The effect was silent -- filenames still matched, so
# searches returned the .md files next door and looked merely "thin" rather than
# broken. Content never got extracted, so no identifier defined in a .ts file
# was findable.
#
# An explicitly wrong mapping is worse than no mapping: unmapped extensions
# (.tsx, .rs, .toml, ...) fall through to libmagic via usesystemfilecommand=1
# and get indexed as text anyway. Only an explicit entry suppresses that.
#
# After changing this file, mimetypes are not re-derived for already-indexed
# files -- their mtime has not changed. Force it for the affected subset:
#   systemctl --user stop recollindex
#   recollindex -r -Z -p '*.ts' ~/Code
#   systemctl --user start recollindex

.ts = text/plain
